# hypernix.countertop API reference

Implementation: `src/hypernix/chat/countertop.py`

## `interactive_cli(use_rich=True) -> int`

Interactive TUI/CLI menu for all HyperNix operations.

## `Countertop()`

A persistent multi-turn chat session bound to an oven.

## `Countertop.authenticate_t1(t1_key) -> Any`

Authenticate and bind a T1 API key to this Countertop session.

## `Countertop.t1_meta() -> Any | None`

Return the authenticated T1 key metadata, if bound.

## `Countertop.t1_stats() -> dict[str, Any]`

Return Gatekeeper usage statistics for the bound T1 key.

## `Countertop.say(user, max_new_tokens=None, temperature=None, top_k=None, top_p=None, seed=None) -> str`

Append ``user`` to the transcript, generate a reply, append

## `Countertop.reset() -> None`

Clear the running transcript (keeps ``system`` and config).

## `Countertop.messages() -> list[dict[str, str]]`

Return the full message list including the system prompt

## `Countertop.render(add_generation_prompt=True) -> str`

Render the current transcript through the chat template

## `countertop(oven, system=None, persona=None, template=None, max_history_tokens=None, bell=None, flour=None, t1_key=None, keymaster=None, gatekeeper=None, **sampling) -> Countertop`

Build a :class:`Countertop`.
